  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-12-07T02:10:58.898Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "After applying VRChat 2024.4.2, the Standard shader set to Cutout becomes opaque due to fallback.\n\n■How to reproduce\n\n・Set StandardShader to “Cutout” and lower the transparency to make it invisible.\n\n・After uploading, apply a safety to the shader from a third-party perspective to check it. Or, turn on fallback shaders from the pie menu.\n\n・It appears opaque.\n\nIn the past, I believe this would have been applied if it were a Cutout, even if it fallback in this manner.\n\nHowever, I cannot distinguish whether this is a glitch or whether it was more of a glitch that it had been functioning correctly until now.",
